{"id":"evs","corpus":"aws","title":"Amazon Elastic VMware Service","sourceUrl":"https://docs.aws.amazon.com/evs/latest/userguide/what-is-evs.html","license":"AWS Documentation © Amazon Web Services, Inc.","blocks":[{"kind":"h1","text":"Amazon Elastic VMware Service"},{"kind":"p","text":"You can use Amazon Elastic VMware Service (Amazon EVS) to deploy and run a VMware Cloud Foundation (VCF) environment directly on EC2 bare metal instances within Amazon Virtual Private Cloud (VPC)."},{"kind":"h2","text":"Features of Amazon EVS"},{"kind":"p","text":"The following are key features of Amazon EVS:"},{"kind":"p","text":"Simplify and accelerate your migration to AWS"},{"kind":"p","text":"Remove migration friction and ensure operational consistency with subscription portability and automated deployment of VMware Cloud Foundation (VCF) in the cloud. Extend on-premises networks and migrate workloads without having to change IP addresses, retrain staff, or re-write operational runbooks."},{"kind":"p","text":"Retain control of your VMware architecture in the cloud"},{"kind":"p","text":"Keep complete control over your VMware architecture and optimize a virtualization stack that meets the unique demands of your applications, including add-ons and third-party solutions."},{"kind":"p","text":"Self-manage or leverage AWS Partners for a managed experience"},{"kind":"p","text":"Unlock choice and flexibility to self-manage, or leverage the expertise of AWS Partners to manage and operate your VCF environment on AWS to meet your business goals across talent, time, and costs."},{"kind":"p","text":"Scale and protect your business from disruptions"},{"kind":"p","text":"Enhance scalability on the most secure, scalable, and resilient cloud for migrating and operating your VMware-based workloads."},{"kind":"p","text":"Embrace AWS innovation to transform your applications and infrastructure"},{"kind":"p","text":"As an AWS-native service, Amazon EVS simplifies extending and expanding your VMware environment with 200+ services (including managed databases, analytics, serverless and containers, and generative AI) to transform your business."},{"kind":"h2","text":"Get started with Amazon EVS"},{"kind":"p","text":"To create your first Amazon EVS environment, see Getting started with Amazon Elastic VMware Service. In general, getting started with Amazon EVS involves completing the following steps."},{"kind":"li","text":"Complete prerequisites. For more information, see Setting up Amazon Elastic VMware Service."},{"kind":"li","text":"Create an Amazon EVS environment. During environment creation, Amazon EVS creates the required VLAN subnets using the CIDR ranges that you specify and adds hosts to the environment."},{"kind":"li","text":"Customize VCF. Configure your environment in the vSphere user interface according to your needs. This may include setting up logins, policies, monitoring, and more."},{"kind":"li","text":"Connect and migrate. Connect your environment to your on-premises data center and migrate your VCF workloads to Amazon EVS."},{"kind":"h2","text":"Accessing Amazon EVS"},{"kind":"p","text":"You can define and configure your Amazon EVS deployments using the following interfaces:"},{"kind":"li","text":"Amazon EVS console - Provides a web interface to create Amazon EVS environments."},{"kind":"li","text":"AWS CLI - Provides commands for a broad set of AWS services and is supported on Windows, macOS, and Linux. For more information, see AWS Command Line Interface."},{"kind":"li","text":"AWS CloudFormation - Provides a specification for each resource type, such as AWS::EVS::Environment. You create a template using the resource specification, and CloudFormation takes care of provisioning and configuring the resources for you."}],"lemmas":{"amazons":["amazon","amazons"],"elastics":["elastic","elastics"],"serviced":["serviced","service"],"servicing":["servicing","service"],"uses":["use","uses"],"used":["used","use"],"deploys":["deploys","deploy"],"deployed